    "answer": "I have updated the map to a **state-by-state heat map** (a choropleth), which is much easier to read at a glance! I removed the 22,000+ individual points and instead grouped the customers by state.\n\nHere is how to read the new map:\n*   **Darkest Purple States:** These are your biggest markets with the highest number of customers (over 600 per state). You can immediately spot powerhouse states like California, Texas, Florida, New York, and Illinois. \n*   **Medium Purple/Pink States:** These states have moderate customer bases (between 170 and 600 customers). This includes a solid band across the Midwest, parts of the South, and the Pacific Northwest.\n*   **Lightest Pink/White States:** These represent regions with fewer than 60 customers each. As you can clearly see, large sections of the Great Plains and Mountain West (like Wyoming, Montana, and the Dakotas) have very little market penetration.\n\nThis view makes it instantly clear which states are driving the business and which ones are largely untapped!"
  },
